# Sample .npmrc for working in zerobias-org sub-repos.
#
# All Zerobias-related NPM scopes (@zerobias-org and the closed-source
# siblings @zerobias-com, @auditmation, @auditlogic) are served by the
# org's private NPM registry at https://pkg.zerobias.org with a single
# token (ZB_TOKEN). Anonymous reads to that registry return 401, so
# `npm install` inside any sub-repo will fail unless ZB_TOKEN is set
# in the environment.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Copy this file:     cp .npmrc.example .npmrc   (or place it in $HOME)
#   2. Set the env var:    export ZB_TOKEN=...
#   3. Run npm install inside any sub-repo as normal.
#
# DO NOT replace ${ZB_TOKEN} with a literal token string.
# DO NOT commit this file as `.npmrc` (it's already in .gitignore).
#
# If you don't have a ZB_TOKEN: you can still read source code, but you
# can't install dependencies or publish. Contact the maintainers if you
# need access for legitimate contribution.

@zerobias-org:registry=https://pkg.zerobias.org/
@zerobias-com:registry=https://pkg.zerobias.org/
@auditmation:registry=https://pkg.zerobias.org/
@auditlogic:registry=https://pkg.zerobias.org/
//pkg.zerobias.org/:_authToken=${ZB_TOKEN}
